# .dockerignore | What `docker build` may see. An ALLOW list: everything is left out, then only the code is let
# back in, so a new secret or data folder can never slip into an image by being forgotten here.
# Milestone 4, step 2. CI checks the built image for leaks as well (.github/workflows/ci.yml, job "image").

# 1. Nothing
*

# 2. The code the server runs, and the files the images are built from
!backend/
!frontend/client/
!API calls/
!main_backend.py
!requirements.txt
!docker/

# 3. Never, even inside the folders above
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.crt
**/*.p12
**/*.db
**/*.db-*
**/*secret*
**/*credentials*
**/*token*.txt
**/passwords_to_hand_out.txt
**/test_users.txt
**/.dramatizer_client.json
**/*.wav
**/*.mp3
**/*.flac
**/*.ogg
**/*.m4a
**/*.aac
**/*.opus
**/*.parquet
**/*.zip
**/*.tar
**/*.tar.gz
**/*.pt
**/*.pth
**/*.safetensors
**/*.onnx
**/*.log
